From 7aa72e4fbcbb178e8f4b146cd060cf088462cfda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:52:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Crawl fixes from Search Console: robots.txt skips /homes/
 listings, and a cold cache holds a page 1.8 s, not 3

Search Console, 2026-11-12: 6,154 noindex listing pages crawled, 30 "crawled, not
indexed" that are all photo-proxy cards, API calls and analyzer links, 5xx and 404s on
listings and filtered searches, and four guides Google had found but never crawled.

- robots.txt: every crawler may read the site except /homes/ (listings, map, filtered
  searches, photo proxy, API), /cdn-cgi/ and ?mls= analyzer links. /homes/ and the
  place pages under /homes/near/ stay open. sitemap-homes.xml is now listed.
- edge.js: the whole page waits at most 1.8 s for listings (was 3 s per step, up to
  three feed steps). A search still running keeps going in the background, so the next
  visitor gets it from the cache; a strip that missed it fills after load.
- idx-test: the slow-CRM controls now require under 2.5 s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0186ha1gzzmbWyPnagoCELMZ
---
 chapter3realty/robots.txt | 33 ++++++++++++---------------------
 idx-lib/edge.js           | 24 ++++++++++++++++--------
 tools/idx-test.mjs        |  4 +++-
 3 files changed, 31 insertions(+), 30 deletions(-)

